    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 022306\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n306 PM PST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n\n* Temperatures will hover within a few degrees of seasonal normals \n  through the week with otherwise quiet conditions.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Sunday.\n\nAfter a very active weekend, calmer conditions are expected for the \nweek ahead with dry conditions, fairly seasonable temperatures, and \ngenerally light winds through at least mid-week. Currently, \nshortwave ridging dominates the region with mostly clear skies and \nlight northwesterly breezes. A quick moving shortwave will push \nthrough the Great Basin on Tuesday-Wednesday, but impacts will be \nminimal across our region aside from some high clouds and minor \nbreezes across the southern Great Basin. Thereafter, stronger \nridging builds into the West allowing for a slow warming trend and \ncontinued clear skies. Strengthening pressure gradients as surface \nhigh pressure builds over the Great Basin will allow for some \nincreasing northerly winds down the Colorado River Valley by Friday \nthrough the weekend, but conditions will remain dry.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Winds \nremain light and follow typical, daily patterns. Chance of 10+ knots \nis 10% or less throughout the TAF period. High clouds increase this \nevening, with bases at or above 20kft.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Northerly breezes weaken \nthis evening as winds return to a light and diurnal pattern across \nmost of the region. These conditions continue on Monday, with the \nexception of our northwestern zones where southerly gusts of 15-25 \nknots are anticipated in the afternoon. VFR conditions persist with \nscattered to broken clouds at or above 15kft.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Outler\nAVIATION...Woods\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
